WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.897
Return to Avery's worktable.

2
00:00:02.037 --> 00:00:05.726
Progress does not mean Avery personally completes every booking.

3
00:00:05.867 --> 00:00:12.425
It means colleagues understand the goal, have useful responsibilities, can raise concerns, and receive support.

4
00:00:12.566 --> 00:00:15.904
The team can test an improvement and learn from what happens.

5
00:00:16.044 --> 00:00:19.483
That is the shift from individual success to team success.

6
00:00:19.624 --> 00:00:25.303
Our pathway connects role transition, trust and communication, shared action, and reflection.

7
00:00:25.443 --> 00:00:30.518
A manager still needs to consider the people, the service, and the evidence in front of them.

8
00:00:30.658 --> 00:00:35.921
Now read The New Manager Challenge and form your own conclusions about Taylor at Westfield.

9
00:00:36.062 --> 00:00:38.637
Separate what the case reports from your assumptions.

10
00:00:38.777 --> 00:00:45.845
Connect your observations to Chapter twenty-one, then justify feasible priorities and explain how they could be carried out.

11
00:00:45.985 --> 00:00:49.941
Do not treat generation labels as an explanation by themselves.

12
00:00:50.081 --> 00:00:54.686
Follow Discussion seven in Canvas for the current requirements and deadlines.

13
00:00:54.827 --> 00:00:57.629
Peer replies are not required for this section.

14
00:00:57.769 --> 00:01:00.685
This lesson and its game are optional and ungraded.

15
00:01:00.825 --> 00:01:05.680
You can review any chapter, read the full transcript, or try Library Loot Drop.

16
00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:08.372
Your case analysis remains your own work.
